            <ArticleTitle>Hybrid method in severe pulmonary embolism not suitable for systemic fibrinolysis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>544-546</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0218492317735722</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute massive pulmonary embolism is known to be associated with high mortality, and treatment options may be limited if systemic fibrinolysis is contraindicated. We report the exciting results of a novel mechanical-pharmacological hybrid approach in 3 patients with life-threatening massive pulmonary embolism, in whom systemic fibrinolysis was contraindicated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
